# PUBLIC_PATHS — the whitelist promoted to the orphan `main` (the public face).
#
# Each non-comment line is a git pathspec relative to the repo root.
# A line beginning with `!` is an *exclude*: a sub-path under an included
# dir that stays dev-only (pruned after extraction).
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# Anything NOT listed here is dev-only and never reaches `main`. `main` is a
# strict path-subset of `dev` — there are no divergent/`main`-only files, so
# always edit public files on `dev` and let `scripts/promote.sh` snapshot them.
#
# Some entries (LICENSE, NOTICE, .env.example) don't exist yet — they're
# authored by C15/C14. promote.sh skips missing whitelist entries with a note.

